    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601">

                <pb facs="0815" n="805" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg805"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/8–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crocker</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-27T17:00:00+01:00">August 27, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1812. Deptel 1366, August 18.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d601-f1"/> British, French
                    and American Missions Saturday<anchor n="34" xml:id="d601-f2"/> presented
                    identical notes to Foreign Office addressed to Salazar<anchor n="34a"
                        xml:id="d601-f3"/> requesting Portuguese Government’s assistance in <pb
                        facs="0816" n="806" xml:id="pg806"/> effecting repatriation of German
                    officials and agents. Director of Political Affairs to whom notes were handed
                    reacted along general lines of Embtel 1577, July 23 but ultimate decision
                    depends on Dr. Salazar and we will press for formal reply. Despatch
                        follows.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d601-f4"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent to Dept, repeated to Madrid as 193, London as 422, Paris as 288.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Crocker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
